Fix (commit a330414e, test-only, two files):
- Both scans drop the content-based NUL skip. Binary files skip by extension
  list only: png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, ico, woff, woff2, ttf, pdf, db,
  sqlite, zip, gz, mp3, mp4, wasm (new BINARY_EXTENSIONS set plus an
  isBinaryPath helper in each file). Text content scans for tokens even when
  it holds a NUL (utf8 read; tokens are ASCII).
- New failing-first style regression case in
  scripts/__tests__/openrouter-s4-adversarial.test.ts
  ("ADV-S4-1 NUL regression"): a temp .ts source with a banned token plus a
  NUL in a comment still reports the hit. It asserts the temp file is not a
  binary path, the read text still holds the NUL, and the scan reports
  exactly ["api.openai.com"].
- No earlier assertion changed. The gate self-check (exact BANNED_TOKENS,
  the directory-only exclusion set, 3 openrouter-only cases) is unchanged
  and still passes.

Breakage proof against the old logic (cheap node check, no new run needed):
a source string with a NUL in a comment plus `api.openai.com` gives
old_logic_hits=0 (old `includes("\0")` skip) vs new_logic_hits=1. The old
logic misses the real hit; the new logic reports it.

Proof on the real repo:
- `npx vitest run --config scripts/vitest.config.ts -t 'openrouter'` exits 0
